W:1. The gypsy rover came over the hill,
W:And down through the valley so shady.
W:He whistled and he sang 'til the green woods rang,
W:and he won~the heart of a lady.
W:
W:Chorus:
W:Ah-de-do, ah-de-do-da-day,
W:Ah-de-do, ah-de day-dee;
W:He whistled and he sang 'til the green woods rang,
W:And he won the heart of a lady.
W:
W:2. She left her father's castle gate.
W:She left her own fine lover.
W:She left her servants and her estate,
W:To follow her gypsy rover.
W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:4. Her father saddled up his fastest stead,
W:And roamed the valley all over.
W:He W:sought his daughter at great speed,
W:And the whistlin' gypsy rover.
W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:5. He came at last to a mansion fine
W:Down by the river Clady.
W:And there was music and there was wine
W:For the gypsy and his lady.
W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:6. "He is no gypsy, my father," said she,
W:"He's Lord of freelands all over.
W:And I will stay 'til my dying day
W:With my whistlin' gypsy rover."
W:(Chorus:)
